md prints an empty array over three lines, `[`, an empty line, then `]`.

Cosmetic, and low priority next to the other markers here: the bytes are valid
JSON and every parser accepts them. It is recorded because a blank line invented
in the middle of machine output is the exact class of thing this suite guards,
and because `[]` is what every other pretty printer emits for an empty array.

The cause is Foundation. ListCommand.renderJSON asks JSONSerialization for
`.prettyPrinted` output, and JSONSerialization renders an empty array as
"[\n\n]" rather than "[]". The fix is to answer "[]" directly when there are no
entries, before reaching JSONSerialization.
